#: kalzium_i18n.cpp:253
msgid ""
"Vulcanization of Rubber. Natural or India rubber, as it was then known, was "
"of limited usefulness to industry. Rubber products melted in hot weather, "
"froze and cracked in cold, and adhered to virtually everything until the day "
"in the mid-19th century when inventor Charles Goodyear accidentally dropped "
"some rubber mixed with sulfur on a hot stove. Goodyear's discovery of what "
"came to be known as vulcanization strengthened rubber so it could be applied "
"to a vast variety of industrial uses, including, eventually, automobile "
"tires."
